---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Digitali terms of service: what you may and may not do with our digital products and this website."
  path="/terms"
>
  <section class="section-tight legal">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width: 780px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>

      <div class="draft-banner" role="note">
        <strong>DRAFT — owner must review before launch.</strong> This is a
        plain-language draft, not legal advice. Items marked [MERCHANT CONFIG]
        must be completed, and a qualified professional should review this
        document for your jurisdiction. Last updated: October 2026.
      </div>

      <p>
        These terms govern your use of this website and of digital products sold
        by [MERCHANT CONFIG: legal company name] ("Digitali", "we", "us").
      </p>

      <h2>1. What we sell</h2>
      <p>
        Digitali sells downloadable digital planning tools as one-time purchases.
        Each product is delivered as a ZIP archive containing a self-contained
        HTML file plus documentation. No physical goods are shipped and no
        subscription is created.
      </p>

      <h2>2. License</h2>
      <p>
        When you purchase a product, you receive a single-user, non-exclusive,
        non-transferable license to use it on your own devices, as described in
        the <a href="/license">Digital Product License</a>. You do not acquire
        ownership of the software itself.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Acceptable use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use the products for your own personal or professional planning.</li>
        <li>
          Do not redistribute, resell, share, upload or publicly display the
          product files.
        </li>
        <li>Do not attempt to circumvent any license or access controls.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Payments</h2>
      <p>
        Payments are processed by Lemon Squeezy as Merchant of Record once
        checkout is activated. Prices are shown in USD and are exclusive of any
        taxes that Lemon Squeezy may be required to collect. We do not store
        payment card details.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Refunds</h2>
      <p>
        Refunds are handled according to our <a href="/refund-policy">Refund
        Policy</a>, which forms part of these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>6. No warranties; your responsibility for backups</h2>
      <p>
        Products are provided "as is". We work hard to make them reliable, but
        we cannot guarantee they are error-free or fit for every purpose. Your
        planning data is stored locally in your browser: you are responsible for
        keeping backups using the built-in export feature. We are not liable for
        data lost because backups were not kept.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, our liability is
        limited to the amount you paid for the product giving rise to the claim.
        Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under applicable consumer
        law that cannot be waived.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. Material changes will be announced on this
        site. Continued use after changes take effect constitutes acceptance.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Governing law and contact</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of [MERCHANT CONFIG: jurisdiction].
        Questions: [MERCHANT CONFIG: contact email].
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
